-- R5, field opening (IMPLICIT-PROPS-DESIGN.md §11.7): two record-typed
-- binders of one rule that share a field name make a bare read of that name
-- ambiguous. The error names both binders, at the read and at the declaration
-- that opened the second; `buyer's name` and `seller's name` both still work.
--
-- Merely sharing the name is fine: `who pays` below opens the same two records
-- and reads them spelled out, and draws no error.

DECLARE Buyer  HAS name IS A STRING
                   pays IS A NUMBER
DECLARE Seller HAS name IS A STRING

GIVEN buyer  IS A Buyer
      seller IS A Seller
GIVETH A STRING
`who signs` MEANS name

GIVEN buyer  IS A Buyer
      seller IS A Seller
GIVETH A STRING
`who pays` MEANS buyer's name

-- A field only one of them has is not a collision.
GIVEN buyer  IS A Buyer
      seller IS A Seller
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how much` MEANS pays
